{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe light here is fading, and I find myself reflecting on the day’s strange juxtapositions. We visited the abattoir, that place of necessary violence, and then the Bourse, where the life of the city pulses in pure abstraction. It is a vivid reminder that the ethical life of the state is not a static ideal, but a living process where spirit externalizes itself into law and economy.\n\nI dined with Cousin and Fauriel. We spoke of Greek folk songs, and I was struck by how the particularity of a people’s history must first be preserved in its art before it can be elevated into universal consciousness. It is a gentle counterpoint to the rigid formalism we often encounter.\n\nMy thoughts are with you and the boys. The journey is tiring, but the spirit of the place is stimulating. I hope Karl and Immanuel are well and that Ludwig is settling into his studies.\n\nYours ever,\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795080532,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":205,"prompt_tokens":957,"total_tokens":1162,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-tObbXqw8HIjdV8PrbPsk4TRjeYeJg4A0","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":957,"prompt_ms":957.6,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.0006269592476489,"prompt_per_second":999.3734335839599,"predicted_n":205,"predicted_ms":4874.481,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.89451470588235,"predicted_per_second":41.85060932640829}}